Implement user story SKY-002-a: Implement SkyscannerClient class with typed interfaces, error handling, and mock mode

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.ts exporting SkyscannerClient class, SearchParams and FlightResult interfaces. Constructor accepts optional apiKey (falls back to RAPIDAPI_KEY env var, throws if neither present/non-empty). searchFlights uses global fetch, throws on 4xx/5xx (status in message, no apiKey leaked), throws on malformed response. Opt-in mock mode: MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns deterministic fixture without fetch call; any other value → real fetch, no silent fallback.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/skyscanner/client.ts exports a SkyscannerClient class whose constructor signature is constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string }); apiKey is stored as a private field (private or # prefix) and is not publicly readable
- SearchParams interface is exported with exactly: origin: string, destination: string, date: string, adults?: number
- FlightResult interface is exported with exactly: price: number, currency: string, airline: string, departure: string, arrival: string, duration: number, stops: number
- searchFlights uses the Node.js global fetch exclusively — no axios, node-fetch, or other HTTP dependency imported
- When no apiKey is passed and RAPIDAPI_KEY is unset or empty-string, or apiKey is passed as empty string (''), constructing SkyscannerClient throws an Error whose message references the missing key; when both constructor apiKey and RAPIDAPI_KEY are present, constructor apiKey takes precedence
- When the API returns a 4xx or 5xx status, searchFlights rejects with an Error that includes the HTTP status code in its message; the Error message must not contain the apiKey value anywhere
- When the API response body is malformed or missing expected fields, searchFlights rejects with a descriptive parse/validation Error
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env var equals exactly 'true', searchFlights resolves with a deterministic, non-empty FlightResult[] fixture (≥2 results, valid shape, varying prices for cheapest-selection in SKY-004) without calling fetch; when MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API is unset, empty, or any value other than 'true' (e.g. 'false', '1', 'TRUE'), searchFlights performs the real fetch call — real HTTP/API failures are NEVER silently replaced with mock/fixture data





